I'm working with an analysis that has several spatial models. I wanted to use Leroux models (implemented in INLA through "besagproper2") but I'm not able to get correct results when I include more than one "besagproper2" model. In the next toy example: 1) the first model gets the correct estimations; 2) model 2, with besagproper2, gives very low estimates for variable "x1" compared to model1; 3) if you execute the models only with one spatial model, it doesn't matter if "x1" or "x2", results are identical for model1 and model2.

Any clue why I have this strange behaviour when I include more than one "besagproper2"?

